--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,46 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Passkeys and account settings
+
+Sign in at `/devtools-times/signin`, create an account at `/devtools-times/signup`,
+and manage your account at `/devtools-times/account/settings`. Account creation
+uses the existing password service, then offers optional passkey enrollment.
+Password sign-in remains available for recovery. Passwords are verified by the
+existing service and are never stored in this application.
+
+The same-origin `/api/auth/*` endpoints use server-side Astro sessions and
+SimpleWebAuthn to verify registration and authentication. Challenges are bound
+to the browser session, expire after five minutes, and are consumed once.
+Reauthentication only accepts the signed-in account's passkeys and requires
+user verification. Sensitive account changes require verification within the
+last five minutes; removing a passkey always prompts for verification in the UI.
+
+Deployment configuration:
+
+- Serve over HTTPS (or localhost for development). Set `AUTH_ORIGIN` to the
+  exact public origin, such as `https://news.example.com`, without a path. The
+  hostname becomes the passkey RP ID. If omitted, the request origin is used for
+  local and preview deployments. Passkeys are tied to that hostname.
+- Set `AUTH_STORE_PATH` to a writable, persistent file path. The default is
+  `.data/auth.json`, excluded from Git. It stores user IDs, credential public
+  keys, counters, labels, timestamps, and pending challenges; never private keys.
+- This sample file store serializes operations in **one Node process**. Before
+  deploying multiple workers or replicas, replace `authTransaction` with a
+  shared transactional database and configure a shared Astro session driver.
+  Preserve both credential data and sessions across application restarts.
+- The Node adapter supplies filesystem session storage by default. Use a
+  persistent session driver for your hosting environment; the session cookie
+  is HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, and Secure in production.
+
+The client uses native WebAuthn APIs with `webauthn-polyfills`, conditional
+autofill, and feature-detected password-manager signals. Known provider names
+and icons are a small local snapshot from the
+[passkey-authenticator-aaguids registry](https://github.com/passkeydeveloper/passkey-authenticator-aaguids).
+Unknown or withheld AAGUIDs use a generic key icon and label. Provider metadata
+is used only for display.
+
+Validation: `pnpm run build` compiles the server and client without starting a
+server. Live password-service responses and authenticator prompts require an
+HTTPS deployment and are not exercised by the build.
